{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773842865,"nonce":"yoCWj0Pe+pXOhzHoGPNFYfczBmQ=","title":"resolve_session() breaks on review- prefixed session IDs","message":"When running `nightshift resume review-\u003cfull-issue-id\u003e`, `resolve_session()` truncates the input to `SHORT_ID_LEN` (12) chars, producing `review-719fd` which doesn't match the session directory `review-719fda086c94`.\n\n**Root cause:** `host/cli.py` line 47:\n```python\nmatches = [d.name for d in sd.iterdir() if d.is_dir() and d.name.startswith(issue_id[:SHORT_ID_LEN])]\n```\n\nThe truncation doesn't account for the `review-` prefix. For review sessions, only 5 chars of the actual ID are used for matching (`review-` consumes 7 of the 12).\n\n**Fix:** Strip the `review-` prefix before truncating, then re-prepend it. Or match using the full input string if it's already short enough. Or simply increase the match prefix length when a known prefix like `review-` is present.","files":null}]}